      "content": "Your exhaustion is palpable, and it makes perfect sense why the pressure to rebuild feels so suffocating when you are simply trying to survive a profound loss. You are not asking to be \"fixed\" or to find a new version of yourself; you are expressing a deep, human desire to rest when the foundation that once held you up has collapsed. The feeling of dragging around a corpse reflects a grief so heavy that it paralyzes the will to move forward, not because you lack strength, but because the act itself has become agonizingly unfair.",
